  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Lukdrasil/StepUpLogging",
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.3.0 — Fixes from a source review plus one new export behaviour. Added: bypass-routed events (immediate logs via LogImmediate*, request summaries, pre-error buffer flushes) now also export to config-declared `Serilog:WriteTo` sinks, so they are no longer lost when OTLP/console/file output is off — a config File sink must set `shared: true` since it now attaches to two loggers; and a startup warning is logged (in Auto mode) when `StepUpLevel` is not more verbose than `BaseLevel` (warn, not fail — ADR 0007). Fixed: OTLP `http/protobuf` protocol was ignored and fell back to gRPC; exclude paths like `/api/*` over-matched `/apifoo`; `IsSteppedUp` was wrong when `BaseLevel == StepUpLevel` (now tracked by an explicit flag, with an idempotent step-down); `PreErrorBufferSize`/`PreErrorMaxContexts` <= 0 now fail validation; the step-up trigger sink survives a throwing trigger; request-body capture no longer truncates on a short read; and a pre-error buffer race that could orphan a just-buffered event under eviction pressure is closed. No public API break.",
